<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n109496" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποφθάνω</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ</span>], aor.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπέφθην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					4.307
				</span></i>
			; part.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποφθάς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					7.144
				</span></i>
			; also in 
				Med.
			
			aor.
			part. (v. infr.): later aor. 1
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπέφθᾰσα</span> (v.
				infr.):—<i>haste before, be</i> or <i>get
				beforehand,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποφθὰς δουρὶ μέσον περόνησεν</span>
			<i>getting beforehand</i> he pierced him through the middle,
			Il.l.c.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔγραψεν ὑποφθάσας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Pomp.</u>
					21
				</span></i>
			:—also in part.
			
				Med.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κτεῖνεν ὑποφθάμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					4.547
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> c. acc.,
				<i>to be beforehand with</i> one, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
			</span></i> l.c., <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Aem.</u>
				26
			</span></i>, etc.:—
				Med.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν ὑποφθαμένη φάτο μῦθον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					15.171
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.227
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Bianor</span>).</div>
